        "original_id": "a1640b0e-b1ec-5976-8125-b4c3f7059b32",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Douglas Morrow, Monty Stratton\n- Works: The Stratton Story\n- Awards: Academy Award\n- Topics: Major League Baseball, disability, hunting accidents\n\nFacts:\n- Monty Franklin Pierce Stratton was born on May 21, 1912.\n- Monty Stratton was nicknamed \"Gander\" for a trick pitch he developed.\n- Monty Stratton was a Major League Baseball pitcher.\n- The 1949 film \"The Stratton Story\" is a biography of baseball player Monty Stratton.\n- Monty Stratton was disabled in a hunting accident.\n- Douglas Morrow earned an Academy Award for his script for the 1949 film \"The Stratton Story\".\n- Monty Franklin Pierce Stratton died on September 29, 1982.",
